WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:02.170
So I won an Emmy.

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:03.170
Here's what that day looked like.

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:07.240
I landed in New York two and a half hours
before the Emmys started, and I was filthy

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.070
because I had been hiking and reporting on
a story in Switzerland for two weeks and I

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.320
hadn't showered.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.580
I also didn't have any clothes for the Emmys.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.120
So first stop was H&amp;M to grab something to
wear.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.830
I snagged a bunch of clothes, most of it off
the sales rack, and headed to my hotel where

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:24.820
I had about 45 minutes to shower and get ready
before heading to the Emmys.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.880
And then I had a random thought about bacteria
living on my body...

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.949
Because I follow John Green on the Internet,
I know that there are trillions of microorganisms

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:34.100
in my body at all time, regardless of how
much soap I use.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.200
Here I am all ready to go.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.780
I hopped on a city bike and booked it just
in time to get to the Emmys.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:40.020
I did the red carpet thing.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:44.760
I pretended I was fancy or something, but
I was not expecting to win until...

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.730
”Blue States, You're the Problem.”

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.620
The New York Times Opinion Video.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:49.620
The New York Times.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.789
[ANNOUNCER]: Accepting the Emmy: Johnny Harris.

00:00:52.789 --> 00:00:54.710
And then I got on stage and gave a little
speech.

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:59.329
So, yeah, that's how I got this big, shiny
trophy and I’m feeling kind of proud about

00:00:59.329 --> 00:00:59.420
it.

